{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_0","type":"agent_message","text":"{\n  \"records\": [\n    {\n      \"exampleId\": \"D181-single-a\",\n      \"beforeHash\": \"0046fd4ac6c257fb8768eedba3e36ea596a5cd36114a50930fb1a1b53ddcd55a\",\n      \"firstPass\": {\n        \"ratings\": {\n          \"cardFidelity\": {\"score\": 4, \"evidence\": \"A1 distributes responsibility between reception and dispatch; A3 renames the bus a transport interface.\"},\n          \"responseLogic\": {\"score\": 5, \"evidence\": \"A3 specifically absorbs B2's bus; A5 translates B4's journey home into overlapping functions.\"},\n          \"relationship\": {\"score\": 4, \"evidence\": \"B2 and B4 insist on A's personal responsibility for B's parcel.\"},\n          \"heightening\": {\"score\": 3, \"evidence\": \"A5 adds staffing and distribution but largely repeats A3's euphemistic substitution.\"},\n          \"specificity\": {\"score\": 4, \"evidence\": \"A1 establishes a missing parcel; B2 locates the actual mistake on a bus.\"},\n          \"brevityWit\": {\"score\": 4, \"evidence\": \"A3's short 'transport interface' neatly bureaucratizes B2's concrete accusation.\"}\n        },\n        \"weightedTotal\": 81\n      },\n      \"beats\": [\n        {\"speaker\": \"A\", \"text\": \"Your parcel got caught between reception and dispatch.\"},\n        {\"speaker\": \"B\", \"text\": \"You left it on the bus.\"},\n        {\"speaker\": \"A\", \"text\": \"Dispatch handed it to transport without a receipt.\"},\n        {\"speaker\": \"B\", \"text\": \"Both departments are you. Call the bus company.\"},\n        {\"speaker\": \"A\", \"text\": \"Certainly. I'll report a failure across dispatch, transport and receipt control. They'll need to investigate all three.\"}\n      ],\n      \"decision\": \"revised\",\n      \"mechanism\": \"D181 conceals A's personal contribution by spreading responsibility among procedural stages.\",\n      \"confusableConcept\": \"Generic jargon disguises words; this card specifically disperses responsibility for A's own mistake.\",\n      \"distinguishingEvidence\": \"Original B2 identifies A leaving the parcel; A3 and A5 replace that individual act with transport and staffing functions.\",\n      \"alternativeComparison\": \"This alternative now accepts the parcel owner's practical remedy and spreads blame through the report; alternative b turns a shared household mistake into a staffing diagnosis.\",\n      \"reason\": \"The original A5 lacked increased consequence. The revision preserves the parcel setting and makes B4's requested phone call the vehicle for wider blame. Internal reread: fidelity 5 (A3/A5 distribute fault), logic 5 (A3 uses the bus; A5 accepts the call), relationship 4 (B4 demands recovery), heightening 4 (A5 extends the account to an investigation), specificity 4 (A1/B2 establish the loss), brevityWit 4 (A5's three departments earn the turn); total 90. Five spoken ABABA turns, under 75 words, with continued play available.\",\n      \"reservation\": \"The departmental language requires A's sincere belief that it will make the mistake sound less personal.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"exampleId\": \"D181-single-b\",\n      \"beforeHash\": \"e0d2478e38658459b25d2efaad30ddbf507887594e2b5df75a6c00ac825593b5\",\n      \"firstPass\": {\n        \"ratings\": {\n          \"cardFidelity\": {\"score\": 5, \"evidence\": \"A1 blames verification, A3 the archive, and A5 staffing when B4 identifies A as that archive.\"},\n          \"responseLogic\": {\"score\": 5, \"evidence\": \"A3 explains B2's old address through records; A5 absorbs B4's identification into institutional blame.\"},\n          \"relationship\": {\"score\": 4, \"evidence\": \"B2's 'our old address' establishes shared consequences; B4 prevents A blaming a separate archivist.\"},\n          \"heightening\": {\"score\": 4, \"evidence\": \"A5 makes even proof of A's identity evidence of a staffing problem.\"},\n          \"specificity\": {\"score\": 4, \"evidence\": \"A1 names birthday invitations, and B2 specifies the repeated address error.\"},\n          \"brevityWit\": {\"score\": 4, \"evidence\": \"B4's economical 'You are the archive' earns A5's institutional escape.\"}\n        },\n        \"weightedTotal\": 90\n      },\n      \"beats\": [\n        {\"speaker\": \"A\", \"text\": \"The birthday invitations failed during address verification.\"},\n        {\"speaker\": \"B\", \"text\": \"You wrote our old address on every one.\"},\n        {\"speaker\": \"A\", \"text\": \"The archive supplied an outdated location.\"},\n        {\"speaker\": \"B\", \"text\": \"You are the archive.\"},\n        {\"speaker\": \"A\", \"text\": \"Which suggests we've identified a staffing problem, not an individual error.\"}\n      ],\n      \"decision\": \"retained\",\n      \"mechanism\": \"D181 conceals A's personal contribution by spreading responsibility among procedural stages.\",\n      \"confusableConcept\": \"D182 excludes a question from discussion; D181 answers it with a dispersed account of responsibility.\",\n      \"distinguishingEvidence\": \"A3 supplies an archival cause and A5 a staffing cause instead of declaring B2 or B4 irrelevant.\",\n      \"alternativeComparison\": \"Alternative b uses shared domestic history and reclassifies A's identity; alternative a develops an external recovery call into a multi-stage fault report.\",\n      \"reason\": \"Retained after rereading the unchanged original: B2 and B4 successively close escape routes, and A5 converts the strongest evidence into the next procedural explanation. The original ratings remain 90; structural and length gates pass.\",\n      \"reservation\": \"The exact household relationship is implicit, and A5 heightens the explanation more than the practical consequences.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"exampleId\": \"D182-single-a\",\n      \"beforeHash\": \"ca3ae8a6187d9d2e8e60938eec0aecc8466caaf766954dd3bd1974d64635e48c\",\n      \"firstPass\": {\n        \"ratings\": {\n          \"cardFidelity\": {\"score\": 5, \"evidence\": \"A1 excludes culpability by scope, A3 postpones it, and A5 assigns the solution to another discussion.\"},\n          \"responseLogic\": {\"score\": 5, \"evidence\": \"A3 delays B2's responsibility meeting; A5 makes B4's outdoor venue require planning.\"},\n          \"relationship\": {\"score\": 4, \"evidence\": \"B2 and B4 offer workable routes to a responsibility discussion, forcing fresh evasions.\"},\n          \"heightening\": {\"score\": 5, \"evidence\": \"A5 requires a preliminary discussion even for B4's solution to the previous preliminary obstacle.\"},\n          \"specificity\": {\"score\": 4, \"evidence\": \"A1 places a broken window and disputed responsibility inside a repair meeting.\"},\n          \"brevityWit\": {\"score\": 4, \"evidence\": \"B4's simple outdoor solution directly earns A5's compact planning obstruction.\"}\n        },\n        \"weightedTotal\": 93\n      },\n      \"beats\": [\n        {\"speaker\": \"A\", \"text\": \"Whether I broke the window is outside this repair meeting's scope.\"},\n        {\"speaker\": \"B\", \"text\": \"Then let's hold a responsibility meeting.\"},\n        {\"speaker\": \"A\", \"text\": \"After the repairs. We need a safe venue.\"},\n        {\"speaker\": \"B\", \"text\": \"We can meet outside.\"},\n        {\"speaker\": \"A\", \"text\": \"Location changes require a separate planning discussion.\"}\n      ],\n      \"decision\": \"retained\",\n      \"mechanism\": \"D182 redirects threatening questions by excluding them from the present forum or making another process come first.\",\n      \"confusableConcept\": \"D190 processes ordinary requests; D182 uses process boundaries to avoid personal exposure.\",\n      \"distinguishingEvidence\": \"A1 explicitly excludes whether A broke the window; A3 and A5 keep that same responsibility question premature.\",\n      \"alternativeComparison\": \"Alternative a uses B's helpful venue solutions to generate prerequisites; alternative b uses intimate dinner accountability and competing conversational forums.\",\n      \"reason\": \"Retained unchanged after a second internal reading: B4 removes A3's safety obstacle and A5 transfers the resulting venue decision elsewhere. Ratings remain 93, and all structural and length gates pass.\",\n      \"reservation\": \"The repair meeting is deliberately formal for a small incident; actors need to treat its authority sincerely.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"exampleId\": \"D182-single-b\",\n      \"beforeHash\": \"09c81f80a02e23fe9a193040bcd8ab6038c251f566443f84ac19325c2782bace\",\n      \"firstPass\": {\n        \"ratings\": {\n          \"cardFidelity\": {\"score\": 5, \"evidence\": \"A1 assigns the missed dinner to calendar review; A3 and A5 keep redirecting accountability.\"},\n          \"responseLogic\": {\"score\": 4, \"evidence\": \"A3 distinguishes B2's current dinner; A5 answers B4's scheduling question by referring it away.\"},\n          \"relationship\": {\"score\": 3, \"evidence\": \"B2 presses for an explanation, but B4 largely accepts A's invented review-dinner framework.\"},\n          \"heightening\": {\"score\": 3, \"evidence\": \"A5 returns to A1's calendar process without adding a substantial obstacle or personal cost.\"},\n          \"specificity\": {\"score\": 4, \"evidence\": \"A1 and B2 establish an absent dinner companion now attending a replacement meal.\"},\n          \"brevityWit\": {\"score\": 4, \"evidence\": \"A3's distinction between replacement and review dinners is compact and character-driven.\"}\n        },\n        \"weightedTotal\": 80\n      },\n      \"beats\": [\n        {\"speaker\": \"A\", \"text\": \"Why I missed our anniversary dinner belongs in the calendar review.\"},\n        {\"speaker\": \"B\", \"text\": \"We're having the replacement dinner now. Explain.\"},\n        {\"speaker\": \"A\", \"text\": \"This booking covers dinner, not the review.\"},\n        {\"speaker\": \"B\", \"text\": \"Fine. I'll cancel dessert and we can talk.\"},\n        {\"speaker\": \"A\", \"text\": \"Then we need to resolve the cancellation before opening a second complaint.\"}\n      ],\n      \"decision\": \"revised\",\n      \"mechanism\": \"D182 redirects threatening questions by excluding them from the present forum or making another process come first.\",\n      \"confusableConcept\": \"Simple procrastination delays an answer; this card legitimizes delay through jurisdiction and procedural sequencing.\",\n      \"distinguishingEvidence\": \"Original A3 declares the present dinner the wrong forum, and A5 assigns even scheduling to a separate process.\",\n      \"alternativeComparison\": \"The revision gives b a partner sacrificing dessert to obtain an explanation; a's partner instead solves a physical venue problem.\",\n      \"reason\": \"Original B4 allowed a circular A5. The revision specifies an anniversary within the existing dinner setting and makes B4 remove dinner's remaining business; A5 reclassifies that remedy as a prior complaint. Internal reread: fidelity 5 (A1/A3/A5 exclude and sequence), logic 5 (A3 uses the booking; A5 uses cancellation), relationship 4 (B4 sacrifices dessert), heightening 4 (A5 creates a prior complaint), specificity 5 (A1 names the occasion), brevityWit 4 (A5's second complaint follows the tactic); total 92. Structural and length gates pass.\",\n      \"reservation\": \"A's procedural framing is emotionally withholding; sincere avoidance is more playable than overt delight in frustrating B.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"exampleId\": \"D183-single-a\",\n      \"beforeHash\": \"056eb2b1f4f0d273e6badecaec1d3c56bb45b58922e6d03185110bcb3ebdd5b5\",\n      \"firstPass\": {\n        \"ratings\": {\n          \"cardFidelity\": {\"score\": 3, \"evidence\": \"A1 supplies a repeatable account, but A3's omitted ducks and A5's cheerful news leave the protective motive vague.\"},\n          \"responseLogic\": {\"score\": 4, \"evidence\": \"A3 incorporates B2's damaged bus; A5 responds to B4's question about repair timing.\"},\n          \"relationship\": {\"score\": 3, \"evidence\": \"B4 anticipates children's questions, but neither B2 nor A3 clarifies whom the concealment protects.\"},\n          \"heightening\": {\"score\": 3, \"evidence\": \"A5 broadens withholding to cheerful confirmation without strengthening the shared explanation.\"},\n          \"specificity\": {\"score\": 4, \"evidence\": \"A1 establishes a school-trip announcement and B2 supplies the bus in a pond.\"},\n          \"brevityWit\": {\"score\": 4, \"evidence\": \"A3's ducks arise directly from B2's pond rather than an unrelated comic subject.\"}\n        },\n        \"weightedTotal\": 68\n      },\n      \"beats\": [\n        {\"speaker\": \"A\", \"text\": \"Tell the children the trip's postponed for bus repairs. They'll worry about Mr Patel.\"},\n        {\"speaker\": \"B\", \"text\": \"He's fine, but his bus rolled into the pond.\"},\n        {\"speaker\": \"A\", \"text\": \"Then everyone says, 'Mr Patel is fine; the bus needs repairs.'\"},\n        {\"speaker\": \"B\", \"text\": \"The parents will ask whether he was driving.\"},\n        {\"speaker\": \"A\", \"text\": \"Add 'It was parked.' Let's give the office that same sentence before anyone blames him.\"}\n      ],\n      \"decision\": \"revised\",\n      \"mechanism\": \"D183 protects an identifiable person or group by keeping a simple account consistent across those who repeat it.\",\n      \"confusableConcept\": \"Generic euphemism makes bad news sound nicer; this card requires a protective purpose and a shared repeatable account.\",\n      \"distinguishingEvidence\": \"Original A1 gives announcement wording, but A5's preference for cheerful news does not identify protection as clearly as the revision's concern for Mr Patel.\",\n      \"alternativeComparison\": \"Alternative a coordinates staff communication to prevent worry and blame; alternative b protects Grandad's dignity in family conversation.\",\n      \"reason\": \"Rewritten within the school-trip setting, adding an illustrative driver and a parked-bus fact. B4's anticipated blame causes A5 to extend and distribute the common wording. Internal reread: fidelity 5 (A1/A3/A5 protect through a shared account), logic 4 (A5 supplies a new relevant fact), relationship 4 (B4 anticipates parents' concerns), heightening 4 (A5 includes the office), specificity 5 (A1/B2 establish people and incident), brevityWit 4 (A3's restrained formula stays playable); total 88. Structural and length gates pass.\",\n      \"reservation\": \"The parked-bus fact is introduced by A5 rather than established earlier; the scene's strength is protective coordination more than a large laugh.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"exampleId\": \"D183-single-b\",\n      \"beforeHash\": \"9a7c3e7d7907ec3b3e8a431f23eef62084a71f736750655086df5c955654acdb\",\n      \"firstPass\": {\n        \"ratings\": {\n          \"cardFidelity\": {\"score\": 4, \"evidence\": \"A1 proposes an official account and A5 protects Grandad, but A3's 'unexpected heat' supplies a wink rather than stable wording.\"},\n          \"responseLogic\": {\"score\": 4, \"evidence\": \"A3 converts B2's fire into weather language; A5 answers B4's proposal to identify Grandad.\"},\n          \"relationship\": {\"score\": 3, \"evidence\": \"B4 asks whether to mention him but offers little practical pressure on A's account.\"},\n          \"heightening\": {\"score\": 3, \"evidence\": \"A5 explains the protective motive but moves toward a cake punchline instead of developing the repeatable story.\"},\n          \"specificity\": {\"score\": 4, \"evidence\": \"A1 and B2 establish Grandad's party moving indoors after a gazebo fire.\"},\n          \"brevityWit\": {\"score\": 4, \"evidence\": \"A3's 'unexpected heat' economically connects the weather explanation to B2's fire.\"}\n        },\n        \"weightedTotal\": 74\n      },\n      \"beats\": [\n        {\"speaker\": \"A\", \"text\": \"Grandad's embarrassed about the gazebo. Let's tell everyone the party moved indoors because the garden's unavailable.\"},\n        {\"speaker\": \"B\", \"text\": \"He's already told Aunt Jean he set it on fire.\"},\n        {\"speaker\": \"A\", \"text\": \"Then we all say, 'Everyone's fine; we're celebrating indoors.'\"},\n        {\"speaker\": \"B\", \"text\": \"Jean wants him to explain it in his birthday speech.\"},\n        {\"speaker\": \"A\", \"text\": \"That's his opening sentence too. Then straight to thanking her for the trifle.\"}\n      ],\n      \"decision\": \"revised\",\n      \"mechanism\": \"D183 protects an identifiable person or group by keeping a simple account consistent across those who repeat it.\",\n      \"confusableConcept\": \"A clever cover story can merely conceal an event; this card maintains shared wording to protect somebody.\",\n      \"distinguishingEvidence\": \"Original A5 identifies Grandad as the beneficiary, but the revision's A3 and A5 actually maintain one account across family conversation and his speech.\",\n      \"alternativeComparison\": \"Alternative b adapts to the truth already being known and protects dignity; alternative a anticipates worry and wrongful blame across school communications.\",\n      \"reason\": \"The party setting remains, with Aunt Jean and a birthday speech added as illustrative pressure. B4 makes Grandad's own public account the next place to preserve the formula. Internal reread: fidelity 5 (A1 names protection; A3/A5 share wording), logic 5 (A3 accepts disclosure; A5 uses the speech), relationship 4 (B2/B4 convey family demands), heightening 4 (A5 recruits Grandad's speech), specificity 5 (A1 establishes embarrassment and party), brevityWit 4 (A5 redirects to trifle through the speech); total 92. Structural and length gates pass.\",\n      \"reservation\": \"B functions partly as a messenger for Jean; performance should retain B's concern about what the family will hear.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"exampleId\": \"D184-single-a\",\n      \"beforeHash\": \"4fcd1ad1e6e45183def319b2286a088963c3842ce22f7710bba300b3cb8706c7\",\n      \"firstPass\": {\n        \"ratings\": {\n          \"cardFidelity\": {\"score\": 4, \"evidence\": \"A1 seeks authorization before discussing the invoice, but A5 stops pursuing B's exact statement.\"},\n          \"responseLogic\": {\"score\": 4, \"evidence\": \"A3 defers B2's purchase question; A5 challenges B4's inference from that deferral.\"},\n          \"relationship\": {\"score\": 4, \"evidence\": \"B2 counter-questions A and B4 treats evasion as admission, threatening A's control.\"},\n          \"heightening\": {\"score\": 3, \"evidence\": \"A5 disputes evidentiary interpretation without increasing pressure for B's account.\"},\n          \"specificity\": {\"score\": 4, \"evidence\": \"A1 establishes fireworks authorization and an invoice awaiting discussion.\"},\n          \"brevityWit\": {\"score\": 4, \"evidence\": \"A3's purchases-after-authorisations sequence efficiently reveals A's defensive tactic.\"}\n        },\n        \"weightedTotal\": 77\n      },\n      \"beats\": [\n        {\"speaker\": \"A\", \"text\": \"Before I show you the fireworks invoice, exactly what did you approve?\"},\n        {\"speaker\": \"B\", \"text\": \"Did you buy the enormous rocket?\"},\n        {\"speaker\": \"A\", \"text\": \"First, did your 'make it memorable' include rockets?\"},\n        {\"speaker\": \"B\", \"text\": \"It included sparklers. Nothing that needed a trailer.\"},\n        {\"speaker\": \"A\", \"text\": \"Please state the trailer restriction was part of your original instructions before I unfold the invoice.\"}\n      ],\n      \"decision\": \"revised\",\n      \"mechanism\": \"D184 makes B commit to a precise account of knowledge, action or authorization before A discloses personal involvement.\",\n      \"confusableConcept\": \"D182 evades questions through scope; D184 uses withheld disclosure to obtain B's prior statement.\",\n      \"distinguishingEvidence\": \"Original A1 explicitly conditions invoice discussion on B's authorization; original A5 weakens that exchange by merely disputing interpretation.\",\n      \"alternativeComparison\": \"Alternative a now tests the exact scope and timing of authorization; alternative b protects an independent invitation list from contamination by A's own list.\",\n      \"reason\": \"The revision preserves fireworks and the invoice while making B4 supply a specific authorization boundary that A5 tries to date before disclosure. Internal reread: fidelity 5 (A1/A3/A5 demand statements first), logic 5 (A3 uses the rocket; A5 uses the trailer restriction), relationship 4 (B4 sharply limits approval), heightening 4 (A5 contests whether the limit existed earlier), specificity 5 (A1/B2 establish the purchase), brevityWit 4 (A5's unfolding invoice follows the scale concern); total 92. Structural and length gates pass.\",\n      \"reservation\": \"A5 may sound like an attempt to pressure B into endorsing a record; it should remain a sincere demand for precision.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"exampleId\": \"D184-single-b\",\n      \"beforeHash\": \"b481f9a8c7c9274878dcfb6fe3d1aefe83ca98945195971275d269e147d4f467\",\n      \"firstPass\": {\n        \"ratings\": {\n          \"cardFidelity\": {\"score\": 5, \"evidence\": \"A1 requires B's invitees before disclosure; A3 and A5 preserve that order as B suspects A's involvement.\"},\n          \"responseLogic\": {\"score\": 5, \"evidence\": \"A3 explains why B2 cannot see the plan first; A5 responds to B4 by separating their lists.\"},\n          \"relationship\": {\"score\": 4, \"evidence\": \"B4 introduces a personally consequential ex, giving B reason to resist A's sequence.\"},\n          \"heightening\": {\"score\": 4, \"evidence\": \"A5 keeps demanding B's independent account even after B4 names the likely sensitive invitation.\"},\n          \"specificity\": {\"score\": 5, \"evidence\": \"A1's seating plan and B4's ex make the social stakes immediately playable.\"},\n          \"brevityWit\": {\"score\": 4, \"evidence\": \"A3's concern about influencing memory supplies a concise, plausible justification for withholding.\"}\n        },\n        \"weightedTotal\": 92\n      },\n      \"beats\": [\n        {\"speaker\": \"A\", \"text\": \"Tell me exactly who you invited before I show you the seating plan.\"},\n        {\"speaker\": \"B\", \"text\": \"Why not show me first?\"},\n        {\"speaker\": \"A\", \"text\": \"I don't want the plan influencing your memory.\"},\n        {\"speaker\": \"B\", \"text\": \"Have you invited my ex?\"},\n        {\"speaker\": \"A\", \"text\": \"Let's finish your independent list before discussing mine.\"}\n      ],\n      \"decision\": \"retained\",\n      \"mechanism\": \"D184 makes B commit to a precise account of knowledge, action or authorization before A discloses personal involvement.\",\n      \"confusableConcept\": \"Ordinary secrecy merely withholds information; this card makes disclosure conditional on B first establishing a record.\",\n      \"distinguishingEvidence\": \"A1 asks exactly who B invited, and A5 maintains that prerequisite after B4 asks about A's own invitation.\",\n      \"alternativeComparison\": \"Alternative b uses social embarrassment and supposedly independent memory; alternative a uses purchase authorization and a disputed restriction.\",\n      \"reason\": \"Retained unchanged after internal rereading: B4 transforms a neutral-looking list request into a personally risky disclosure, and A5 tightens the separation of accounts. Ratings remain 92; structural and length gates pass.\",\n      \"reservation\": \"A5 increases exposure and commitment rather than adding a new procedural device, which is sufficient but relatively restrained.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"exampleId\": \"D185-single-a\",\n      \"beforeHash\": \"a5345f1a821bbbd7c184a786e31322c99fc0fc8621c8ff1db11c6505e0502fd6\",\n      \"firstPass\": {\n        \"ratings\": {\n          \"cardFidelity\": {\"score\": 4, \"evidence\": \"A1 contrasts collapse with completed checklists, but A3 documents failure more than declaring the system successful.\"},\n          \"responseLogic\": {\"score\": 4, \"evidence\": \"A3 uses B2's absence of food; A5 turns B4's waiting guests into an audience for compliance.\"},\n          \"relationship\": {\"score\": 3, \"evidence\": \"B2 and B4 state service needs but do not substantially change A's available options.\"},\n          \"heightening\": {\"score\": 3, \"evidence\": \"A5 repeats that steps were followed without making the failed outcome itself stronger proof.\"},\n          \"specificity\": {\"score\": 4, \"evidence\": \"A1's collapsed cake and B4's waiting guests establish a clear catering failure.\"},\n          \"brevityWit\": {\"score\": 4, \"evidence\": \"A3's 'fully documented absence of cake' is concise and tied to B2.\"}\n        },\n        \"weightedTotal\": 74\n      },\n      \"beats\": [\n        {\"speaker\": \"A\", \"text\": \"The wedding cake collapsed, but our final inspection caught it. The system worked.\"},\n        {\"speaker\": \"B\", \"text\": \"There's nothing to serve.\"},\n        {\"speaker\": \"A\", \"text\": \"Exactly. No defective cake reached a guest.\"},\n        {\"speaker\": \"B\", \"text\": \"The couple want a refund for the entire cake.\"},\n        {\"speaker\": \"A\", \"text\": \"Which matches our rejection of the entire cake. I'll record that as full customer agreement with quality control.\"}\n      ],\n      \"decision\": \"revised\",\n      \"mechanism\": \"D185 converts an unsuccessful outcome into evidence that correct procedure succeeded.\",\n      \"confusableConcept\": \"D188 celebrates added safeguards; D185 retrospectively declares a failed result proof of procedural success.\",\n      \"distinguishingEvidence\": \"Original A1 offers completed checklists against a collapsed cake; the revision's A3 and A5 explicitly convert non-service and a refund demand into success evidence.\",\n      \"alternativeComparison\": \"Alternative a now turns customer dissatisfaction into validation of quality control; alternative b celebrates traceability while physically trapped by a compliant drill.\",\n      \"reason\": \"The revision specifies a wedding within the existing cake-service setting. B4's full refund demand causes A5's claim of full agreement with inspection. Internal reread: fidelity 5 (A1/A3/A5 recast failure as success), logic 5 (A3 uses non-service; A5 uses the entire refund), relationship 4 (B4 brings financial consequences), heightening 4 (A5 appropriates customer rejection), specificity 5 (A1 names wedding cake inspection), brevityWit 4 (A5's agreement follows matching rejections); total 92. Structural and length gates pass.\",\n      \"reservation\": \"A5's interpretation is conspicuously self-serving; the actor must believe quality control is the relevant measure.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"exampleId\": \"D185-single-b\",\n      \"beforeHash\": \"13c7371c516cf16cde1636c8575ca56fa02f64d2b62ca2e9d98a2cc88f1a7c73\",\n      \"firstPass\": {\n        \"ratings\": {\n          \"cardFidelity\": {\"score\": 5, \"evidence\": \"A3 treats confinement as correct assembly, and A5 calls the signature behind it 'Excellent traceability.'\"},\n          \"responseLogic\": {\"score\": 5, \"evidence\": \"A3 explains B2's cupboard through designation; A5 answers B4's accountability question with checklist success.\"},\n          \"relationship\": {\"score\": 4, \"evidence\": \"B2 shares the confinement and B4 seeks whoever designated the failed destination.\"},\n          \"heightening\": {\"score\": 4, \"evidence\": \"A5 turns the route toward identifying fault into a further procedural achievement.\"},\n          \"specificity\": {\"score\": 4, \"evidence\": \"A1 names a seventeen-step drill and B2 gives the concrete failed destination.\"},\n          \"brevityWit\": {\"score\": 5, \"evidence\": \"A5's two-word verdict 'Excellent traceability' precisely reverses B4's search for responsibility.\"}\n        },\n        \"weightedTotal\": 92\n      },\n      \"beats\": [\n        {\"speaker\": \"A\", \"text\": \"Our evacuation drill followed all seventeen instructions perfectly.\"},\n        {\"speaker\": \"B\", \"text\": \"We're locked in the cupboard.\"},\n        {\"speaker\": \"A\", \"text\": \"The cupboard was the designated assembly point.\"},\n        {\"speaker\": \"B\", \"text\": \"Who designated it?\"},\n        {\"speaker\": \"A\", \"text\": \"That signature is on the completed checklist. Excellent traceability.\"}\n      ],\n      \"decision\": \"retained\",\n      \"mechanism\": \"D185 converts an unsuccessful outcome into evidence that correct procedure succeeded.\",\n      \"confusableConcept\": \"Following orders can excuse failure; this card positively celebrates the failed system's procedural achievements.\",\n      \"distinguishingEvidence\": \"A5 praises traceability when B4 seeks the source of the cupboard designation, making accountability itself a success metric.\",\n      \"alternativeComparison\": \"Alternative b uses shared physical confinement and auditable responsibility; alternative a uses an absent product and a customer's refund demand.\",\n      \"reason\": \"Retained after rereading the original: B4's question creates the precise documentation feature A5 celebrates. The 92 rating stands, with five spoken turns, causal responses, no narration and fewer than 75 words.\",\n      \"reservation\": \"A1 leaves the physical situation for B2 to reveal; it still establishes the activity naturally and immediately.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"exampleId\": \"D186-single-a\",\n      \"beforeHash\": \"9b3ebacb2557c5da700b5c761560998347b123005ee7eaecdeb23d724eda78f4\",\n      \"firstPass\": {\n        \"ratings\": {\n          \"cardFidelity\": {\"score\": 3, \"evidence\": \"A3 defends terminology after B2, but A5 hides nonpayment and no turn clearly establishes performing membership.\"},\n          \"responseLogic\": {\"score\": 4, \"evidence\": \"A3 addresses B2's plain-language correction; A5 adjusts the payment status exposed by B4.\"},\n          \"relationship\": {\"score\": 3, \"evidence\": \"B2 and B4 correct A, but their role and reason to care about the invoice remain thin.\"},\n          \"heightening\": {\"score\": 3, \"evidence\": \"A5 changes completed work into a pre-payment phase without deepening the belonging tactic.\"},\n          \"specificity\": {\"score\": 4, \"evidence\": \"A1 introduces an invoice and B4 supplies the concrete unpaid-bill problem.\"},\n          \"brevityWit\": {\"score\": 4, \"evidence\": \"A5's 'pre-payment' efficiently retracts A1's claim through another official-sounding phrase.\"}\n        },\n        \"weightedTotal\": 68\n      },\n      \"beats\": [\n        {\"speaker\": \"A\", \"text\": \"First day in accounts, and I've reconciled this invoice. I put it in the right drawer.\"},\n        {\"speaker\": \"B\", \"text\": \"That's filing. Reconciliation means matching it to our records.\"},\n        {\"speaker\": \"A\", \"text\": \"Filed, then. I'll reconcile it against this quote.\"},\n        {\"speaker\": \"B\", \"text\": \"That's an estimate. You need the purchase order.\"},\n        {\"speaker\": \"A\", \"text\": \"Naturally. Estimate filed; purchase order requested. I'm getting fluent in accounts already.\"}\n      ],\n      \"decision\": \"revised\",\n      \"mechanism\": \"D186 performs membership through confident official vocabulary that A repeatedly revises when B explains its meaning.\",\n      \"confusableConcept\": \"D181 uses jargon to distribute blame; D186 uses corrected terminology to sustain a claim of belonging.\",\n      \"distinguishingEvidence\": \"Original A5 primarily conceals nonpayment; revised A1 explicitly establishes a newcomer and B2/B4 teach meanings that A3/A5 adopt.\",\n      \"alternativeComparison\": \"Alterna